"""Business rules for the {{ module_title }} module.

Rules that are not shape. Pydantic already rejects a value of the wrong type
or length; what it cannot see is the rest of the table or the current state of
the row being changed. Those checks live here.

Two properties make this worth a package rather than an `if` in the service:
the rule has a name a domain expert would recognise, and a test can call it
with a stub instead of building a service first.

Each rule raises the framework error the HTTP layer already serialises, so a
violation reaches the client as problem+json instead of a 500.
"""

